// Title: Process Launched Without Image Name
// Sigma ID: f208d6d8-d83a-4c2c-960d-877c37da84e5
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Matt Anderson (Huntress)
// Date: 2024-07-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detect the use of processes with no name (".exe"), which can be used to evade Image-based
//   detections.
// False positives:
//   - Rare legitimate software.
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/fake-browser-updates-lead-to-boinc-volunteer-computing-software
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_no_image_name.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\.exe"
